              <tr><td><code>_ga</code></td><td>Google Analytics, only if GA4 enabled</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Distinguishes users for analytics</td><td>Default 2 years</td><td>First-party cookie used by Google tag</td><td>Optional</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</code></td><td>Google Analytics, only if GA4 enabled</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Persists session state</td><td>Default 2 years</td><td>First-party cookie used by Google tag</td><td>Optional</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Google Ads identifiers / tag storage</td><td>Google, only if Ads or conversion tagging enabled</td><td>Marketing / Advertising</td><td>Conversion measurement, advertising attribution and potentially personalisation</td><td>Implementation dependent</td><td>First or third party depending on implementation</td><td>Optional</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Meta Pixel / Meta Business Tools identifiers</td><td>Meta, only if Meta Pixel enabled</td><td>Marketing / Social</td><td>Advertising measurement, audience creation, attribution and retargeting</td><td>Provider dependent</td><td>May involve first- and third-party identifiers</td><td>Optional</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Social plugin technologies</td><td>Meta or another social provider, only if embedded</td><td>Social / Functional / Marketing</td><td>Embedded social functionality and, depending on provider, measurement</td><td>Provider dependent</td><td>Third-party</td><td>Optional unless strictly needed for a requested feature</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Payment session/device technologies</td><td>Razorpay, only if Razorpay enabled</td><td>Strictly Necessary / Security</td><td>Secure payment sessions, browser or device recognition, service operation and fraud/security</td><td>Session or persistent; provider controlled</td><td>Third-party payment environment</td><td>Necessary when that payment service is selected</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Payment/checkout technologies</td><td>PayU, only if PayU enabled</td><td>Strictly Necessary / Security</td><td>Payment checkout, transaction processing and technical or fraud functionality</td><td>Provider controlled</td><td>Third-party payment environment</td><td>Necessary when that payment service is selected</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Courier/tracking cookies</td><td>Shiprocket, DHL or another courier, only where its web tracker is accessed or embedded</td><td>Functional / Necessary on provider service</td><td>Shipment tracking, technical administration and session functionality</td><td>Provider dependent</td><td>Usually third-party on provider domain</td><td>Conditional</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Consent-preference storage</td><td>Shopify / CMP</td><td>Strictly Necessary</td><td>Records whether analytics, marketing and preference processing has been accepted or rejected</td><td>Configure proportionately; Shopify mechanism may evolve</td><td>First-party / platform-managed</td><td>Required for consent system</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3>Important Shopify Discrepancy to Account For</h3>
        <p>Shopify's June 2026 public Cookie Policy still displays several historical merchant-storefront cookie names, but Shopify's own developer changelog says some of those cookies have already been retired.</p>
        <p>Do not list the following as active Grey Exim cookies merely because they still appear in a generic Shopify table:</p>
        <div class="grey-cookie-policy__table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Legacy Shopify cookie status" tabindex="0">
          <table class="grey-cookie-policy__table grey-cookie-policy__table--compact">
            <thead><tr><th>Legacy Shopify cookie</th><th>2026 status</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><code>_tracking_consent</code></td><td>Shopify announced it would stop being set from 15 September 2025; use Customer Privacy API.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>_landing_page</code></td><td>Shopify announced it would stop being set from 15 September 2025.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>_orig_referrer</code></td><td>Shopify announced it would stop being set from 15 September 2025.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>_shopify_s</code></td><td>Shopify announced it would stop being set from 1 January 2026.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><code>_shopify_y</code></td><td>Shopify announced it would stop being set from 1 January 2026.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>This is why Grey Exim's public table describes current or typical technologies subject to live configuration, and why a developer should perform a cookie and pixel scan whenever Shopify or installed apps materially change.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="consent-experience" class="grey-policy__section grey-cookie-policy__appendix">
        <p class="grey-cookie-policy__appendix-label">Appendix B</p>
        <h2><span>B</span> Consent Banner and Preference Experience</h2>
        <p>For the banner itself, Grey Exim should not publish the old wording: <q>By continuing to use our site, you agree to the use of cookies&hellip;</q></p>
        <p>Current consent standards in stricter jurisdictions require a positive action for non-essential cookies rather than mere continued browsing. Shopify likewise instructs developers to record consent only after actual visitor interaction.</p>

        <h3>Recommended First-Layer Banner</h3>
        <div class="grey-cookie-policy__banner-example">
          <strong>Your Privacy Choices</strong>
          <p>We and our partners, including Shopify, use necessary cookies and similar technologies to operate Grey Exim, including our shopping cart, checkout, security and customer-account features. With your permission where required, we may also use preference, analytics, advertising and social-media technologies to understand website use, improve your shopping experience and measure or personalise marketing. You can accept optional technologies, reject non-essential technologies, or manage your preferences. See our Cookie Policy and Privacy Policy for more information.</p>
          <div class="grey-cookie-policy__button-row" aria-label="Example cookie banner actions">
            <span>Accept All</span><span>Reject Non-Essential</span><span>Manage Preferences</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>This wording is consistent with Shopify's recommendation that merchants using a third-party consent platform identify Shopify and explain that cookies or similar technologies may be used for analytics, advertising and personalisation subject to customer consent.</p>

        <h3>Recommended Second-Layer Preference Centre</h3>
        <div class="grey-cookie-policy__preference-list">
          <div><strong>Strictly Necessary &mdash; Always Active</strong><p>Required to securely operate Grey Exim, maintain your shopping cart, support checkout, authenticate sessions, prevent fraud, remember privacy choices and provide functions you request.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Functional</strong><p>Enable optional website functions that make the store easier to use. Turning these off may affect certain optional features.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Preferences</strong><p>Remember choices such as language, currency, country or other shopping preferences.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Analytics &amp; Performance</strong><p>Help us understand how visitors use Grey Exim, which pages or products are viewed and how our website performs so that we can improve the shopping experience.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Marketing &amp; Advertising</strong><p>Help us measure campaigns, understand advertising performance and, where enabled, provide more relevant advertising.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Social Media</strong><p>Enable social-media integrations and, where applicable, social-media measurement or advertising technologies. Advertising-related social tracking will remain off unless the relevant permission is available.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p>Shopify's API supports separate preferences, analytics and marketing signals and lets developers check whether each form of processing is currently allowed based on consent, store configuration and visitor region.</p>

        <h3>Consent Duration and Refresh</h3>
        <p>There is no sensible reason for Grey Exim to ask customers about cookies on every page view. The consent decision should be stored for a proportionate period and shown again when necessary&mdash;for example, after material changes in tracking purposes, when the previous preference expires, when no choice exists for the browser or device, or where applicable requirements call for renewed choice.</p>
        <p>For a practical implementation, a consent preference period of approximately six to twelve months is defensible as a configuration choice, but it should not be described as a universal statutory Indian deadline. The actual duration should be configured in the Shopify or CMP implementation and documented in the technical inventory.</p>

        <h3>Google Configuration</h3>
        <p>Where Google Analytics or Google Ads is installed, Grey Exim should map the preferences interface to Google's current Consent Mode signals:</p>
        <div class="grey-cookie-policy__table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Google Consent Mode mapping" tabindex="0">
          <table class="grey-cookie-policy__table grey-cookie-policy__table--compact">
            <thead><tr><th>Grey Exim selection</th><th>Google setting</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Analytics accepted</td><td><code>analytics_storage = granted</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Analytics rejected</td><td><code>analytics_storage = denied</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Advertising accepted</td><td><code>ad_storage = granted</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Advertising user data accepted</td><td><code>ad_user_data = granted</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Ad personalisation accepted</td><td><code>ad_personalization = granted</code></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Marketing rejected</td><td>Relevant advertising settings = <code>denied</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Google states that consent defaults should be established before measurement commands use the relevant consent information, and then updated after the visitor makes or changes a choice.</p>

        <h3>Meta Configuration</h3>
        <p>Where Meta Pixel is installed, it should be inventoried as a Marketing or Social technology rather than treated as strictly necessary. Meta describes the Pixel as one of its Business Tools and explains that Meta can receive information from third-party websites using its technologies for advertising and measurement purposes.</p>
        <p>A social-media icon that merely links to Grey Exim's Instagram or Facebook page is not equivalent to installing the Meta Pixel. The policy and banner should describe the technology actually deployed, not the social platform merely because Grey Exim has an account there.</p>

        <h3>Cookie Preference Management Instructions for Customers</h3>
        <p>The website should provide a permanent Cookie Preferences link in the footer. Shopify permits merchants to configure customer privacy through <strong>Shopify Admin &rarr; Settings &rarr; Customer privacy</strong>, and its privacy infrastructure can allow preferences to be revisited after the original decision.</p>
        <p>Customers should be told that they can also:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>use Grey Exim's Cookie Preferences control;</li>
          <li>delete or block cookies through their browser;</li>
          <li>change Google or Meta privacy controls directly with those providers where applicable;</li>
          <li>use supported browser privacy signals; and</li>
          <li>withdraw optional consent without losing access to basic product browsing and purchasing functionality, except where blocking a genuinely necessary technology prevents a requested ecommerce operation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Blocking all cookies through the browser can break cart, checkout, login and other functionality because necessary cookies may also be blocked.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="consent-flow" class="grey-policy__section grey-cookie-policy__appendix">
        <p class="grey-cookie-policy__appendix-label">Appendix C</p>
        <h2><span>C</span> Consent Flow</h2>
        <p>The following flow is the recommended technical and UX architecture for Grey Exim. It keeps essential ecommerce technologies available while preventing optional processing from being treated as consented merely because a visitor landed on the site.</p>
        <div class="grey-cookie-policy__flow" aria-label="Recommended consent flow">
          <div><strong>Visitor arrives</strong><p>Load necessary ecommerce and consent storage only.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Privacy choice</strong><p>Show choices when required by region and configuration.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Record consent</strong><p>Accept all, reject non-essential or save category preferences.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Apply permissions</strong><p>Allow only analytics, marketing and preference processing that is permitted.</p></div>
          <div><strong>Revisit choices</strong><p>Let customers reopen Cookie Preferences and change future processing.</p></div>
        </div>
        <p>A developer should not directly read or alter Shopify's internal cookies to implement this flow. Shopify's current API documentation directs developers to the Customer Privacy API, including <code>setTrackingConsent()</code> and methods that determine whether analytics, marketing or preference processing is permitted.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="implementation-checklist" class="grey-policy__section grey-cookie-policy__appendix">
        <p class="grey-cookie-policy__appendix-label">Appendix D</p>
        <h2><span>D</span> Developer Implementation Checklist</h2>
        <p>This policy becomes defensible only when the website behaves the way the text says it behaves. A policy cannot compensate for a Meta or Google pixel that loads before the user's configured choice, an outdated Shopify script or an undisclosed app.</p>
        <div class="grey-policy__callout"><p><strong>The most important technical rule for Grey Exim in 2026:</strong></p><p>Do not write the policy first and then assume the website complies. Configure the website, identify the real technologies, make optional trackers obey the recorded choices and keep the published cookie inventory synchronised with that technical reality.</p></div>
        <div class="grey-cookie-policy__table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Developer implementation checklist" tabindex="0">
          <table class="grey-cookie-policy__table grey-cookie-policy__table--checklist">
            <thead><tr><th>Priority</th><th>Developer action</th><th>Required outcome</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Open Shopify Admin &rarr; Settings &rarr; Customer privacy and audit current configuration.</td><td>Confirm regions, banner, preferences and Shopify privacy settings are intentional.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Audit Settings &rarr; Customer events and every app or custom pixel.</td><td>Identify all Shopify Web Pixels, app pixels and custom pixels.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Remove any direct dependency on <code>_tracking_consent</code>, <code>_shopify_s</code>, <code>_shopify_y</code>, <code>_landing_page</code> or <code>_orig_referrer</code>.</td><td>Stop relying on Shopify storefront cookies officially deprecated for 2025 or 2026.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Use Shopify Customer Privacy API instead of manually editing Shopify cookies.</td><td>Follow Shopify's documented privacy interface.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Implement Accept All, Reject Non-Essential and Manage Preferences.</td><td>Avoid implied or continued-browsing consent for optional tracking.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Default optional categories appropriately before relevant pixels run.</td><td>Avoid pre-consent advertising or analytics where consent is required.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Check Google Analytics installation.</td><td>If GA4 is active, disclose <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;container-id&gt;</code> and map analytics choice to consent state.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Check Google Ads and conversion tags.</td><td>If active, classify as Marketing or Advertising and integrate advertising consent signals.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority">Critical</span></td><td>Check Meta Pixel.</td><td>If active, classify as optional Marketing or Social tracking and ensure it follows marketing consent.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Audit payment gateways.</td><td>Confirm whether Grey Exim actually uses Razorpay, PayU, Shopify or Shop Pay, or another provider before listing it as active.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Audit courier and tracking integrations.</td><td>Distinguish transmitting shipping data from embedding a courier web tracker.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Add a permanent Cookie Preferences link to the footer.</td><td>Allow customers to revisit their choices.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Persist consent with date, version and category information.</td><td>Maintain evidence of the privacy decision associated with the current policy or banner version.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Test checkout after rejecting optional cookies.</td><td>Keep cart, login and checkout functional where they depend only on necessary technologies.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Test consent from a UK or EEA region simulation if Grey Exim accepts those markets.</td><td>Verify regional banner behaviour and supported active-market settings.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Configure Google tags through Consent Mode where Google tools are active.</td><td>Verify default and updated analytics and advertising permissions.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Review browser privacy signals.</td><td>Confirm handling of GPC in configured data-sale or sharing opt-out regions.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Standardise <code>info@greyexim.com</code> across privacy communications.</td><td>Avoid conflicting privacy contact points.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--high">High</span></td><td>Confirm the published grievance contact remains current.</td><td>Keep Hemil Jitendrabhai Makwana's name and Grievance Officer designation accurate.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--medium">Medium</span></td><td>Perform quarterly or material-change cookie and pixel audits.</td><td>Keep the inventory aligned with Shopify and installed-app changes.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--medium">Medium</span></td><td>Maintain a vendor register.</td><td>Record provider, purpose, category, data involved, processing location, retention, consent dependency and review date.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><span class="grey-cookie-policy__priority grey-cookie-policy__priority--medium">Medium</span></td><td>Maintain security and incident-response procedures.</td><td>Support secure ecommerce operation and appropriate incident handling.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

